            Full text: ffmpeg/LICENSE.txt in the installation folder.
Version:    n9.0.2-36-g6882969ce9 (release/9.0 branch)
Build:      BtbN FFmpeg-Builds, variant "win64-lgpl-shared"
            https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/tag/autobuild-2026-10-25-13-00
Website:    https://ffmpeg.org/

How Konvert uses FFmpeg
    FFmpeg runs as a separate program (child process). Konvert does not link to
    it. The FFmpeg files are installed unmodified in the "ffmpeg" folder of the
    installation directory and can be replaced by the user with any compatible
    build (same file names), as permitted by the LGPL.

Build configuration
    The build is configured without --enable-gpl and without --enable-nonfree,
    so it contains no GPL-only component (no libx264, libx265, libxvid) and no
    non-free component (no libfdk-aac). It uses --enable-version3, which is why
    the license is LGPL version 3 or later. The exact configuration is printed
    by `ffmpeg -version`.

    Libraries included in the build relevant to Konvert (each under its own
    LGPL-compatible license): LAME (MP3, LGPL), libopus (BSD), libvorbis (BSD),
    libvpx (BSD), SVT-AV1 (BSD-3-Clause-Clear), OpenH264 (BSD-2-Clause),
    libaom (BSD), dav1d (BSD).

